## Architecture (gridz.bio)

### Read path
`app/[subject]/page.tsx` → `loadGrid()` → Base RPC + `GRIDZ_RESOLVER` direct `text()` / `cellAttestation()` (`lib/loadGridResolver.ts`). No wallet required.

### Publish path (current production)
1. User signs EIP-712 in browser (`ProfileEditor` → `buildProfileGrid`)
2. `POST /api/publish` with signed grid (`app/api/publish/route.ts`)
3. Server registrar wallet: EAS `attest` + `setCellAttestation` per changed cell (`lib/publishEas.ts`, `mode: "registrar"`)
4. User does **not** pay gas; registrar must hold Base ETH

Alternative `mode: "owner"` (user-paid) exists in `publishEas.ts` but editor uses API path.

### Edit / claim permissions
`lib/canEditProfile.ts` + `ProfilePage.tsx`:
- No on-chain grid → anyone can claim
- Local draft in browser → can edit
- Registrar-only on-chain cells (`isRegistrarOnlyPublish`) → reclaimable
- Else → wallet must match cell attester (`isProfileOwner`)

`NEXT_PUBLIC_REGISTRAR_ADDRESS` must match registrar for incomplete-claim detection.

### Demo profile
`demo.gridz.eth` — Elon Musk widget showcase (`scripts/__fixtures__/demoProfile.ts`). Refresh: `pnpm demo:publish` (needs `GRIDZ_SIGNER_KEY` + registrar key). Verify: `pnpm demo:verify`.

## Env vars (root `.env` → Vercel)

| Var | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| `GRIDZ_CHAIN_ID` | `8453` |
| `GRIDZ_RPC_URL` | Base RPC |
| `GRIDZ_RESOLVER` | Resolver proxy (server) |
| `EAS_ADDRESS` / `CELL_SCHEMA` | Server publish |
| `REGISTRAR_PRIVATE_KEY` or `DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY` | `/api/publish` signer |
| `GRIDZ_SIGNER_KEY` | Demo profile signer only |
| `ONECLAW_CHAIN_ID` | Must match `GRIDZ_CHAIN_ID` (`8453`) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` | Client: resolver, chain, RPC, registrar address, WC project id |

**Sync local → next-app:** `pnpm bootstrap` (writes `examples/next-app/.env.local`).

**Sync local → Vercel:** `set -a && source .env && set +a && node scripts/push-vercel-env.mjs`

Never commit `.env` or keys. `push-vercel-env.mjs` derives `REGISTRAR_PRIVATE_KEY` from `DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY` if unset and sets `NEXT_PUBLIC_REGISTRAR_ADDRESS`.

## Chain helpers (add new networks here)

- `scripts/lib/constants.mjs` — `NETWORKS` (mainnet, sepolia, **base**)
- `scripts/lib/gridzChain.mjs` — viem chain for scripts
- `examples/next-app/lib/gridzChain.ts` — wagmi + app
- `examples/next-app/lib/gridzDeployments.ts` — doc/UI constants (env overrides with Base defaults)
- `examples/next-app/lib/wagmiConfig.ts` — single active chain from `NEXT_PUBLIC_GRIDZ_CHAIN_ID`

Pattern: `chainId === 11155111 ? sepolia : chainId === 8453 ? base : mainnet` — never hardcode mainnet-only.

## Sync matrix — when you change X, update Y and run Z

### Contract / chain / addresses
Update **all** of:
1. `specs/deployments.md` (canonical)
2. `examples/next-app/lib/gridzDeployments.ts`
3. `contracts/README.md`
4. `examples/next-app/app/docs/toolkit/page.tsx`, `app/docs/api/page.tsx`
5. `examples/next-app/app/for-ai/page.tsx`
6. `examples/next-app/lib/forAiContent.ts` (`buildLlmsTxt`, `buildSkillMd`) — **escape backticks** inside template literals as `\``
7. `scripts/lib/constants.mjs` if network preset changes
8. Root `.env` → `pnpm bootstrap` → `node scripts/push-vercel-env.mjs`
9. On new chain: `node scripts/register-cell-schema.mjs` before first attest
10. Deploy/upgrade: `contracts/script/Deploy.s.sol` or `Upgrade.s.sol` with `PROXY_ADDRESS`

Run: `cd contracts && forge test` · `pnpm demo:publish` · `pnpm demo:verify`

### Publish flow (editor / API / gas model)
Update:
- `examples/next-app/components/ProfileEditor.tsx` (API vs client `publishEas`)
- `examples/next-app/app/api/publish/route.ts`
- `examples/next-app/components/PublishProgress.tsx` + `.test.tsx`
- `examples/next-app/lib/publishEstimate.ts` + `.test.ts`
- Docs: `app/docs/api/page.tsx`, `claim/page.tsx`, `using-gridz/page.tsx`
- `lib/forAiContent.ts` guardrails + publish workflow

Run: `pnpm --filter gridz-next-app test && pnpm --filter gridz-next-app build`

### Profile permissions / claim UI
Update: `lib/canEditProfile.ts` + `.test.ts`, `components/ProfilePage.tsx`

### Packages (`@gridz/*` or `gridz` Python)
- TS: `packages/` submodule — commit & push gridz-js, bump superproject
- Py: `python/gridz` — `python3 -m venv .venv && pip install -e ".[dev]" && pytest`
- Cross-runtime: `tests/cross-runtime/`

### Docs / agents
Human docs: `examples/next-app/app/docs/**`
Machine: `lib/forAiContent.ts` → `/llms.txt`, `/skill.md`, `/for-ai` (cached routes)
After forAiContent edits: build next-app (template literal syntax breaks easily)

## Commands to run after substantive changes

```bash
# Fast path (gridz.bio only)
pnpm --filter gridz-next-app test
pnpm --filter gridz-next-app build

# Contracts
cd contracts && forge test

# Python core
cd python/gridz && .venv/bin/pytest -q   # create .venv if missing

# Full monorepo (slow)
pnpm check
pnpm check:nomock   # no invented demo data outside __fixtures__

# Demo on-chain smoke
pnpm demo:publish && pnpm demo:verify
```

## Ship to production checklist

1. Tests + build green (above)
2. Commit **examples** → push `gridz-examples`
3. If contracts changed: commit **contracts** → push `gridz-contracts`
4. Commit **gridz** superproject (submodule pointers + `specs/`, `scripts/`)
5. `source .env && node scripts/push-vercel-env.mjs`
6. `vercel --prod` from repo root (aliases `gridz.bio`)
7. Smoke: `curl https://gridz.bio/api/profile/demo.gridz.eth` → `ok: true`, 20 cells

Only commit when user asks. Never force-push main. Never commit secrets.

